  "title": "gsm_{a_rr,rlcmac}: improve handling of GAMMA and P0 fields",
  "description": "As per 3GPP TS 44.060, Table 11.2.29.2 \"PACKET UPLINK ASSIGNMENT information element details\", both GAMMA and P0 fields are encoded in units of 2 dB. So far only `hf_gsm_a_rr_gamma` (`gsm_a.rr.gamma`) was implemented correctly. This MR adds a custom formatter (`fmt_2db_units()`), fixes `hf_gamma` (`gsm_rlcmac.dl.gamma`) and `hf_p0` (`gsm_rlcmac.dl.p0`) in `packet-gsm_rlcmac.c`, and `hf_gsm_a_rr_p0` (`gsm_a.rr.p0`) in `packet-gsm_a_rr.c`.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
